I go to a spice stall.
An old shopkeeper is there.
I say to him, "Namaste Chacha."
He smiles happily.
He shows a tea masala powder.
He says, "Please smell this."
He gives a little powder in my hand.
I smell it.
The aroma is very good!
I say, "Wow, this is excellent."
"What is its price?"
Chacha says, "Fifty rupees."
I say, "I want one small packet."
"Please give it."
He gives one small packet.
I give fifty rupees.
I place that packet in my bag.
